#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166747 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166585 :question/id #uuid "285e2f4a-e8d0-5f5e-a2d2-fe5ba8476358" :question/math-academy-id "e-8256" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\cos(xy), x=t,$ and $y=e^t,$ compute $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}f}{\\textrm{d}t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x = x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}f}{\\textrm{d}t} \n= \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{\\textrm{d}t} + \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy),\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t{e}^{t}), \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t{e}^{t}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=1,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}={e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =[-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t{e}^{t})]\\cdot 1+[-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t{e}^{t})]\\cdot {e}^{t} \\\\  & =-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t{e}^{t})-t{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t{e}^{t}) \\\\  & =-(1+t){e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t{e}^{t}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ed13b87-51ab-547d-a9ed-960eda7db24e" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048707 :topic/math-academy-id 1929 :topic/title "Introduction to Partial Derivatives"}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561381 :question-generator/id #uuid "4f3229b7-d188-5de9-bf1b-a0c92e77f8fd" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186166747.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167326 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c7d16f8-21b4-57d7-b847-6cbf8aec3e45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3t+2{t}^{4}){e}^{{t}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478816} {:answer/id #uuid "a796782b-7f7c-5c6c-8be9-0d882da5296e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2t+3{t}^{4}){e}^{{t}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478834} {:answer/id #uuid "cae71365-386c-58a4-9a23-5f12d23921f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2+{t}^{2}){e}^{{t}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478884} {:answer/id #uuid "e885c723-0ce8-5f1e-ad99-55ec7b846c3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2+3{t}^{3}){e}^{{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478920} {:answer/id #uuid "fba666e9-d566-570e-bbc3-a41fcf8b4194" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3t+2{t}^{3}){e}^{{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478952}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a796782b-7f7c-5c6c-8be9-0d882da5296e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2t+3{t}^{4}){e}^{{t}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478834} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9b1652d-93ab-5313-9296-f0aa0f63c08f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165165}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "284d40a1-d125-53c0-b06b-70dfdac633d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-94587" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x{e}^{xy},x={t}^{2},$ and $y=t,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={e}^{xy}+xy{e}^{xy},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={x}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & ={e}^{{t}^{2}\\cdot t}+{t}^{2}\\cdot t{e}^{{t}^{2}\\cdot t}={e}^{{t}^{3}}+{t}^{3}{e}^{{t}^{3}}=(1+{t}^{3}){e}^{{t}^{3}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =({t}^{2})^{2}{e}^{{t}^{2}\\cdot t}={t}^{4}{e}^{{t}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=2t,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =(1+{t}^{3}){e}^{{t}^{3}}\\cdot 2t+{t}^{4}{e}^{{t}^{3}}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =(2t+2{t}^{4}){e}^{{t}^{3}}+{t}^{4}{e}^{{t}^{3}} \\\\  & =(2t+3{t}^{4}){e}^{{t}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167331 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7aa7cb58-130b-52e2-9ffc-cc9e52330663" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+2\\operatorname{csc}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358818} {:answer/id #uuid "a1a9cb0c-c43b-5a83-8c67-e7c35f7eae70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{csc}⁡t-\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359161} {:answer/id #uuid "ea13c98f-b638-5d97-8167-fa566662cb6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359835} {:answer/id #uuid "ec49dc46-0ba5-5fda-b9c2-6bec956ac528" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cot}⁡t-\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359856} {:answer/id #uuid "f7162188-93f3-50e1-8684-87bec1a6cf00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡t-\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec49dc46-0ba5-5fda-b9c2-6bec956ac528" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cot}⁡t-\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359856} :answer-field/id #uuid "a955c8c5-959c-5957-86ce-5b5f4f04ba90" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360295}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "19a64e51-db17-58fb-852b-340494362842" :question/math-academy-id "q-95078" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x{y}^{2}),x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ and $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$ for $0<t<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x{y}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{x},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{2xy}{x{y}^{2}}=\\frac{2}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}+2\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cot}⁡t-\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284666 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "546085f7-b447-560f-8e03-5f9f83d6f2d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282406} {:answer/id #uuid "74f33be1-f6b9-527c-9c36-b38596ce0f41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282688} {:answer/id #uuid "8d6ac22c-45ee-5e02-aa23-fa2d93a62a90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282915} {:answer/id #uuid "8d8a9385-1ddd-50d1-9fa6-1227b2a8f619" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282916} {:answer/id #uuid "91107c67-4b51-563a-9b9f-7ec21682f202" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d6ac22c-45ee-5e02-aa23-fa2d93a62a90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282915} :answer-field/id #uuid "db0740db-ef2c-573e-a13f-6da541dd04e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284317}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2f247252-c196-59cb-b56b-5c53685b26d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-170668" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,x={t}^{2},$ and $y=t,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t), \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=2t,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\cdot 2t+(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360551 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0906d5df-95ee-50f2-a42b-09e69555e339" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4t(1+2t){e}^{{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357833} {:answer/id #uuid "140ea72d-9a0d-57b5-b67c-2049bb317343" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{t}^{2}(1+{t}^{2}){e}^{{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357925} {:answer/id #uuid "9cea513d-612f-5290-b731-384d792ca237" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8t(1+{t}^{2}){e}^{{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359124} {:answer/id #uuid "c0ba0846-4e92-5a2d-b302-7d756aa55faa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{t}^{3}(2+t){e}^{{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359440} {:answer/id #uuid "e95d1d3f-a370-59d0-97ce-9062ff9fd3d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4t(2+t){e}^{{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359826}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9cea513d-612f-5290-b731-384d792ca237" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8t(1+{t}^{2}){e}^{{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359124} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9bfd21b-4c44-5c5c-ba56-5fadb4ae0273" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360377}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4d8c80e5-aa7d-56a9-83f4-b1c7ab4b5caf" :question/math-academy-id "q-95076" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)={x}^{2}{e}^{y},x=2t$ and $y={t}^{2},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x{e}^{y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={x}^{2}{e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2(2t){e}^{{t}^{2}}=4t{e}^{{t}^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =(2t)^{2}{e}^{{t}^{2}}=4{t}^{2}{e}^{{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=2,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =4t{e}^{{t}^{2}}\\cdot 2+4{t}^{2}{e}^{{t}^{2}}\\cdot 2t \\\\  & =8t{e}^{{t}^{2}}+8{t}^{3}{e}^{{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =8t(1+{t}^{2}){e}^{{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360552 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1830bf59-5084-598f-b1f6-81191dfbfbcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2+t}{\\sqrt{t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357965} {:answer/id #uuid "26a1cc25-ba10-5462-a7f5-4b6c422818d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358100} {:answer/id #uuid "72ac5140-e75a-5b93-834e-7afad4225743" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358751} {:answer/id #uuid "8cdd033a-0457-5b60-bc47-43fcb08320c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+\\sqrt{t}}{\\sqrt{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358978} {:answer/id #uuid "8ddb28d7-a49c-5dad-b528-bbf182a53bcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358988}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ddb28d7-a49c-5dad-b528-bbf182a53bcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358988} :answer-field/id #uuid "146b2117-94cd-5963-92fa-afe7f73a78f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360033}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e0f22ddd-635a-5638-92e4-fbad8751067f" :question/math-academy-id "q-95077" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{2xy},x=t$ and $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{2xy}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2xy}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=1,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}\\cdot 1+\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360553 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "181e483e-0db4-5bd1-964b-afa6fc2ecf27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+4t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357963} {:answer/id #uuid "719dcb03-d975-5054-b48a-74dd57cccf20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358745} {:answer/id #uuid "76fada7e-bbdf-508e-9127-190df8ac22e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358776} {:answer/id #uuid "81dec9c1-74ca-5c5c-9366-b27ffa80a962" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358886} {:answer/id #uuid "c17c2336-706c-5cd5-8b88-2ef24b3288c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-4t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359450}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "719dcb03-d975-5054-b48a-74dd57cccf20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358745} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee046ec2-08f8-5c58-bfb3-059a2ba841f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360423}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7bb11d2f-2294-5c9e-b733-36535d04471b" :question/math-academy-id "q-95079" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,x=4t$ and $y=t,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-4t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=4,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot 4+(-4t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360554 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5774d438-8549-5c81-9843-45d115052cfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2s{e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358513} {:answer/id #uuid "63dc5334-1342-5ac0-8adc-34168c5ef7c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(s+2){e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358624} {:answer/id #uuid "97245f20-2357-5a46-9419-5584f26e4952" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(s+1){e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359074} {:answer/id #uuid "bc07b503-6a18-5c74-b532-0d144efdccab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s(s+2){e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359386} {:answer/id #uuid "c201f1bf-9034-567f-9849-2029c4f2719a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{s}^{2}{e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97245f20-2357-5a46-9419-5584f26e4952" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(s+1){e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359074} :answer-field/id #uuid "1991f021-d4bd-5ba5-9a63-d5673c4d3078" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360037}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "40900f6f-b4af-5c59-b5c2-386989d530fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-95080" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)={e}^{x+2y},x={s}^{2},$ and $y=s,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/7e/7e5b5001794ecdf2c9b9e9102f334a63d2c59bc6f7511c2eb7fa358fc94cb0c5.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $s,$ where $x=x(s)$ and $y=y(s),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={e}^{x+2y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2{e}^{x+2y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & ={e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =2{e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}=2s,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s} \\\\  & ={e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}\\cdot 2s+2{e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2s{e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}+2{e}^{{s}^{2}+2s} \\\\  & =2(s+1){e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360555 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46f944b8-e799-5036-80f1-5ba5c1a7411f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358364} {:answer/id #uuid "82479d60-5437-50e5-882f-1cefac414e6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358893} {:answer/id #uuid "f1724fb0-eb83-58dc-8a3f-92689c7862c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359901} {:answer/id #uuid "fe84e3ca-9757-54b8-a1da-085a92705bae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359990} {:answer/id #uuid "fede68b1-836b-57e9-a83f-57bb56eb0c3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359994}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82479d60-5437-50e5-882f-1cefac414e6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358893} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef608987-b651-5ccb-b9c8-ffdc510994e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360424}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b0e7724b-5745-517d-9a70-23d66bdba953" :question/math-academy-id "q-95081" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=y+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y,\\,x=s$ and $y=2s,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/7e/7e5b5001794ecdf2c9b9e9102f334a63d2c59bc6f7511c2eb7fa358fc94cb0c5.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $s,$ where $x=x(s)$ and $y=y(s),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=1+\\frac{x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2s, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =1+\\frac{s}{2s}=\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}=1,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2s\\cdot 1+\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360556 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b80e388-89f0-55d3-9647-29eb1e7d21a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{csc}^{2}⁡2s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357986} {:answer/id #uuid "2931a144-34bf-5b91-9fd0-2c8561636d73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡2s+{csc}^{2}⁡2s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358129} {:answer/id #uuid "5f982da7-fadd-5a18-83b3-b5af485d42fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡2s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358586} {:answer/id #uuid "981660b8-6d8e-5d6b-a353-cc9e60ac0aac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡2s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359084} {:answer/id #uuid "d2b01e60-3c8a-5b80-ab36-ad8a68a5308f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{sec}^{2}⁡2s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b80e388-89f0-55d3-9647-29eb1e7d21a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{csc}^{2}⁡2s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357986} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce0a50c8-6fe1-52e2-992d-16da1ca6ce29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360348}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f22cdf5c-424c-5c09-91c4-a4b6bd7748c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-95084" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\frac{x}{y},x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s$ and $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/7e/7e5b5001794ecdf2c9b9e9102f334a63d2c59bc6f7511c2eb7fa358fc94cb0c5.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $s,$ where $x=x(s)$ and $y=y(s),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{1}{y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s}{{sin}^{2}⁡2s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s}\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s)+(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s}{{sin}^{2}⁡2s})\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s \\\\  & =-2-2\\cdot \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡2s}{{sin}^{2}⁡2s} \\\\  & =-2-2{cot}^{2}⁡2s \\\\  & =-2{csc}^{2}⁡2s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360557 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cdc706a-1707-5c09-affb-248453b8b3de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2+{s}^{2}}{1+s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357857} {:answer/id #uuid "154db3be-7d69-5ebc-979b-f406345e0c58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s(1-s)}{(1+s)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357939} {:answer/id #uuid "1cc9a21b-0849-5652-a19d-cd8b9c45a0a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{s}^{2}(2+s)}{(1+s)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358001} {:answer/id #uuid "7cec9aba-8f27-55a0-917c-38e83d5f0aee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+{s}^{2}}{(1+s)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358838} {:answer/id #uuid "e28edfdb-62cd-569f-b9f0-d31cb58213f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s(2+s)}{(1+s)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e28edfdb-62cd-569f-b9f0-d31cb58213f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s(2+s)}{(1+s)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359756} :answer-field/id #uuid "083d442a-f627-5528-9841-283282543ad1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360012}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8a57f510-aa58-5248-9a92-0fa5039eed64" :question/math-academy-id "q-95085" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\frac{x}{1+y},$ $x={s}^{2}$ and $y=s,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/7e/7e5b5001794ecdf2c9b9e9102f334a63d2c59bc6f7511c2eb7fa358fc94cb0c5.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $s,$ where $x=x(s)$ and $y=y(s),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{1}{1+y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-\\frac{x}{(1+y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{1}{1+s}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-\\frac{{s}^{2}}{(1+s)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}=2s,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+s}\\cdot 2s-\\frac{{s}^{2}}{(1+s)^{2}}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{2s}{1+s}-\\frac{{s}^{2}}{(1+s)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2s(1+s)-{s}^{2}}{(1+s)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{s(2+s)}{(1+s)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383607 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97cfef0b-b2e9-52d1-81b0-399192df2eb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383609} {:answer/id #uuid "4bd4c4de-e1e5-5ff6-83aa-88f43410589b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t){e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383610} {:answer/id #uuid "a4d046f0-8479-5ddd-8e29-9cf04c57ccd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t){e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383611} {:answer/id #uuid "6cf412ac-5ff2-5717-972e-75f25275ddc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+1){e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383612} {:answer/id #uuid "9e75a459-147f-5daa-8fd7-55841122ff55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bd4c4de-e1e5-5ff6-83aa-88f43410589b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t){e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383610} :answer-field/id #uuid "614acb07-1733-5745-addd-2f741b4bd7c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383608}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5274ee67-b6e6-57da-a682-d2ddd4bf1256" :question/math-academy-id "q-170669" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)={e}^{2y-x},x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ and $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-{e}^{2y-x},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2{e}^{2y-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =-{e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =2{e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =-{e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+2{e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t){e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385838 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "247ee7d0-904c-5d01-8297-06a98015037c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{s}}){e}^{\\sqrt{s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385840} {:answer/id #uuid "7cec0dc1-33bb-5f04-a034-05527df9b19d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+s){e}^{\\sqrt{s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385841} {:answer/id #uuid "323b91bd-668a-507d-8f83-8a04b4f2b115" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2+\\sqrt{s}){e}^{\\sqrt{s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385842} {:answer/id #uuid "ffd6bb8a-7411-5765-b787-90052e6b40f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{s}}){e}^{\\sqrt{s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385843} {:answer/id #uuid "0fbb05f2-b967-534b-9feb-494c22d63500" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+\\frac{\\sqrt{s}}{2}){e}^{\\sqrt{s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fbb05f2-b967-534b-9feb-494c22d63500" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+\\frac{\\sqrt{s}}{2}){e}^{\\sqrt{s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385844} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f70704d-2718-514e-b670-1b5ed75416ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385839}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c583feca-7024-59b3-b46e-988493997541" :question/math-academy-id "q-95083" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=y{e}^{x},$ $x=\\sqrt{s}$ and $y=s,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s}$ for $s>0.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/7e/7e5b5001794ecdf2c9b9e9102f334a63d2c59bc6f7511c2eb7fa358fc94cb0c5.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $s,$ where $x=x(s)$ and $y=y(s),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y{e}^{x},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =s{e}^{\\sqrt{s}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & ={e}^{\\sqrt{s}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{s}},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s} \\\\  & =s{e}^{\\sqrt{s}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{s}}+{e}^{\\sqrt{s}}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{s}}{2}{e}^{\\sqrt{s}}+{e}^{\\sqrt{s}} \\\\  & =(1+\\frac{\\sqrt{s}}{2}){e}^{\\sqrt{s}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561317 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20f072ba-3739-59c5-8fe5-2f46c587a6d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 (t - 1) ((t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} + (t - 3) (t - 1)^{3} + 1) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561322} {:answer/id #uuid "41b0fbc7-8241-50ca-a1fc-d7076693e183" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(t - 1)^{4} (2 t - 6) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561333} {:answer/id #uuid "5feae69f-7c55-5950-b155-315e04edd13d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2 t - 2) ((t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}} + e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561343} {:answer/id #uuid "aa16c309-d04e-5cf3-a65a-db91906040c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (t - 1)^{4} (2 t - 6) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}} + (2 t - 2) ((t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}} + e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561359} {:answer/id #uuid "fa5f5b0e-4b3f-59bf-9b46-043cd0723f33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 (t - 1) ((t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} + (t - 3) (t - 1)^{3} + 1) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20f072ba-3739-59c5-8fe5-2f46c587a6d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 (t - 1) ((t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} + (t - 3) (t - 1)^{3} + 1) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561322} :answer-field/id #uuid "e738eb49-c04b-5d64-84fd-1070608d69a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561376}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "16bb4028-8696-5e87-8e7c-7e1a33c5c4cc" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x e^{x y},$ $x=(t - 1)^{2}$ and $y=(t - 3)^{2},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=x y e^{x y} + e^{x y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x^{2} e^{x y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}} + e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =(t - 1)^{4} e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} &=2 t - 2,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=2 t - 6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =((t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}} + e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}})\\cdot (2 t - 2)+((t - 1)^{4} e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}})\\cdot (2 t - 6) \\\\  & =(2 t - 2) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}} + ((t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} (2 t - 2) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}) + ((t - 1)^{4} (2 t - 6) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}) \\\\  & =2 (t - 1) ((t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} + (t - 3) (t - 1)^{3} + 1) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561328 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41376f0b-fddb-515b-9135-0dcfd4896483" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 27 t^{10} e^{3 t^{7}} + 12 t^{3} (3 t^{7} e^{3 t^{7}} + e^{3 t^{7}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561332} {:answer/id #uuid "6df73b83-3780-5113-98c9-ae7f6c812078" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 t^{3} (3 t^{7} e^{3 t^{7}} + e^{3 t^{7}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561346} {:answer/id #uuid "809bb840-826d-5090-ab24-5ba97394b73e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27 t^{10} e^{3 t^{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561353} {:answer/id #uuid "811d9993-cbf5-58f2-82af-df6589b0f550" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 t^{3} (21 t^{7} + 4) e^{3 t^{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561354} {:answer/id #uuid "e92b5772-4089-5199-9617-602bbe124f77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 t^{3} (21 t^{7} + 4) e^{3 t^{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "811d9993-cbf5-58f2-82af-df6589b0f550" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 t^{3} (21 t^{7} + 4) e^{3 t^{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561354} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a990c52-96e6-5a56-8e2a-37b3d1997675" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561319}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "379f3d57-a4e8-5653-a290-2e107a7dab3c" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x e^{x y},$ $x=3 t^{4}$ and $y=t^{3},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=x y e^{x y} + e^{x y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x^{2} e^{x y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =3 t^{7} e^{3 t^{7}} + e^{3 t^{7}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =9 t^{8} e^{3 t^{7}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} &=12 t^{3},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=3 t^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =(3 t^{7} e^{3 t^{7}} + e^{3 t^{7}})\\cdot (12 t^{3})+(9 t^{8} e^{3 t^{7}})\\cdot (3 t^{2}) \\\\  & =12 t^{3} e^{3 t^{7}} + (36 t^{10} e^{3 t^{7}}) + (27 t^{10} e^{3 t^{7}}) \\\\  & =3 t^{3} (21 t^{7} + 4) e^{3 t^{7}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561337 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1849c99c-ec5f-564e-bd00-2693ebbb1567" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- t^{2} (5 t^{5} + 3) e^{t^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561318} {:answer/id #uuid "212f23b1-5655-5afe-ac3f-c0a1b51cbabf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 t^{7} e^{t^{5}} + 3 t^{2} (t^{5} e^{t^{5}} + e^{t^{5}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561323} {:answer/id #uuid "4b78b10d-4899-5250-a89d-b0ffe4794c07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 t^{7} e^{t^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561339} {:answer/id #uuid "77c6e33f-6d12-5c5d-b983-ae5efd0acca4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t^{2} (5 t^{5} + 3) e^{t^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561351} {:answer/id #uuid "9928a079-eba2-5e28-93d4-777658d1302b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 t^{2} (t^{5} e^{t^{5}} + e^{t^{5}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77c6e33f-6d12-5c5d-b983-ae5efd0acca4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t^{2} (5 t^{5} + 3) e^{t^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561351} :answer-field/id #uuid "03c9cabd-fbbb-5023-88c9-3c2c7ba49282" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561312}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4946f9ea-a5fa-50ee-8aec-931b80816d77" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x e^{x y},$ $x=t^{3}$ and $y=t^{2},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=x y e^{x y} + e^{x y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x^{2} e^{x y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =t^{5} e^{t^{5}} + e^{t^{5}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =t^{6} e^{t^{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} &=3 t^{2},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=2 t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =(t^{5} e^{t^{5}} + e^{t^{5}})\\cdot (3 t^{2})+(t^{6} e^{t^{5}})\\cdot (2 t) \\\\  & =3 t^{2} e^{t^{5}} + (3 t^{7} e^{t^{5}}) + (2 t^{7} e^{t^{5}}) \\\\  & =t^{2} (5 t^{5} + 3) e^{t^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561348 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c83790c-a703-5058-8cbf-04d4152546fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (3 t + 2)^{4} (18 t + 12) e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}} + (18 t + 12) ((3 t + 2)^{4} e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}} + e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561320} {:answer/id #uuid "4509ef26-9cd8-5023-a2e9-3e0842651cf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(18 t + 12) ((3 t + 2)^{4} e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}} + e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561336} {:answer/id #uuid "9218d13e-7ce3-5386-9247-59aab07237b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 (3 t + 2) (2 (3 t + 2)^{4} + 1) e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561356} {:answer/id #uuid "b67e6ad5-a679-54e7-8ac2-2efd98b370e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3 t + 2)^{4} (18 t + 12) e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561362} {:answer/id #uuid "ddfe92d1-9dd2-5418-af08-95dd922c1931" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 (3 t + 2) (2 (3 t + 2)^{4} + 1) e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ddfe92d1-9dd2-5418-af08-95dd922c1931" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 (3 t + 2) (2 (3 t + 2)^{4} + 1) e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561372} :answer-field/id #uuid "30d27a3a-17ea-543d-b1a0-88e5b60881b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561327}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6ff56f6d-0609-54ae-950b-f994f207b14c" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x e^{x y},$ $x=(3 t + 2)^{2}$ and $y=(3 t + 2)^{2},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=x y e^{x y} + e^{x y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x^{2} e^{x y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =(3 t + 2)^{4} e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}} + e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =(3 t + 2)^{4} e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} &=18 t + 12,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=18 t + 12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =((3 t + 2)^{4} e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}} + e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}})\\cdot (18 t + 12)+((3 t + 2)^{4} e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}})\\cdot (18 t + 12) \\\\  & =(18 t + 12) e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}} + ((3 t + 2)^{4} (18 t + 12) e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}}) + ((3 t + 2)^{4} (18 t + 12) e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}}) \\\\  & =6 (3 t + 2) (2 (3 t + 2)^{4} + 1) e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561352 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0753e31c-5005-5a9b-a87b-f91a8c8a77a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 t (2 t^{5} e^{2 t^{5}} + e^{2 t^{5}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561313} {:answer/id #uuid "447c7f99-fdb6-5457-8d9a-e3aa9f50861f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 t^{6} e^{2 t^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561335} {:answer/id #uuid "60fde45f-357e-58f4-affa-c5ef9a2b31ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 t^{6} e^{2 t^{5}} + 4 t (2 t^{5} e^{2 t^{5}} + e^{2 t^{5}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561344} {:answer/id #uuid "d5960284-1fb4-5fe6-a6cc-93c721a5098b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 t (5 t^{5} + 1) e^{2 t^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561371} {:answer/id #uuid "e8702b54-5e62-56c8-9256-f605b63609ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 t (5 t^{5} + 1) e^{2 t^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561378}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8702b54-5e62-56c8-9256-f605b63609ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 t (5 t^{5} + 1) e^{2 t^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561378} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3d976a4-de41-5ed3-b5d4-88d3dc494011" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561375}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "77e86c5a-4b57-5eb8-8644-abcaf34b69bc" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x e^{x y},$ $x=2 t^{2}$ and $y=t^{3},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=x y e^{x y} + e^{x y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x^{2} e^{x y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2 t^{5} e^{2 t^{5}} + e^{2 t^{5}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =4 t^{4} e^{2 t^{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} &=4 t,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=3 t^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =(2 t^{5} e^{2 t^{5}} + e^{2 t^{5}})\\cdot (4 t)+(4 t^{4} e^{2 t^{5}})\\cdot (3 t^{2}) \\\\  & =4 t e^{2 t^{5}} + (8 t^{6} e^{2 t^{5}}) + (12 t^{6} e^{2 t^{5}}) \\\\  & =4 t (5 t^{5} + 1) e^{2 t^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561355 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12df19e5-92b7-5d33-8757-cda8739d3e6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 (3 t + 2) ((3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2} + (3 t - 2) (3 t + 2)^{3} + 1) e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561315} {:answer/id #uuid "545d27d9-3cfd-5eeb-aea7-0eab883c4b69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (3 t + 2)^{4} (18 t - 12) e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}} + (18 t + 12) ((3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2} e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}} + e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561340} {:answer/id #uuid "5b75c05a-d660-5abe-a52d-9ab9e3a38c8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 (3 t + 2) ((3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2} + (3 t - 2) (3 t + 2)^{3} + 1) e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561342} {:answer/id #uuid "aba30610-805a-5061-a2ce-fde43245da17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3 t + 2)^{4} (18 t - 12) e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561360} {:answer/id #uuid "bf49f816-92b6-5bc8-a43f-a220f9f453a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(18 t + 12) ((3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2} e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}} + e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12df19e5-92b7-5d33-8757-cda8739d3e6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 (3 t + 2) ((3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2} + (3 t - 2) (3 t + 2)^{3} + 1) e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561315} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1775f0e-8e1b-5b4b-9760-0645558c6cf5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561367}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8d01c121-a85c-5572-ac96-07c83af29d68" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x e^{x y},$ $x=(3 t + 2)^{2}$ and $y=(3 t - 2)^{2},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=x y e^{x y} + e^{x y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x^{2} e^{x y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2} e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}} + e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =(3 t + 2)^{4} e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} &=18 t + 12,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=18 t - 12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =((3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2} e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}} + e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}})\\cdot (18 t + 12)+((3 t + 2)^{4} e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}})\\cdot (18 t - 12) \\\\  & =(18 t + 12) e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}} + ((3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2} (18 t + 12) e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}}) + ((3 t + 2)^{4} (18 t - 12) e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}}) \\\\  & =6 (3 t + 2) ((3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2} + (3 t - 2) (3 t + 2)^{3} + 1) e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561364 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e1c7a8e-0422-5233-b088-e2341346c984" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 8 t (12 t^{6} + 1) e^{4 t^{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561321} {:answer/id #uuid "5b61d18a-70d2-5b67-a497-85ceecaad618" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 t (4 t^{6} e^{4 t^{6}} + e^{4 t^{6}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561341} {:answer/id #uuid "6f1b3dcf-deeb-5278-88c3-40be3d31308c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64 t^{7} e^{4 t^{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561347} {:answer/id #uuid "774a3c97-56bd-5fbe-bf9f-4aa50c321d1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 t (12 t^{6} + 1) e^{4 t^{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561350} {:answer/id #uuid "e024a943-4b21-5e6c-99ff-b264cf508bf5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 64 t^{7} e^{4 t^{6}} + 8 t (4 t^{6} e^{4 t^{6}} + e^{4 t^{6}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "774a3c97-56bd-5fbe-bf9f-4aa50c321d1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 t (12 t^{6} + 1) e^{4 t^{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561350} :answer-field/id #uuid "b48d05a5-03ed-527d-b03e-d22708b9e3bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561361}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ba6447ed-c55a-5176-ab21-a18af111a0e0" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x e^{x y},$ $x=4 t^{2}$ and $y=t^{4},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=x y e^{x y} + e^{x y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x^{2} e^{x y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =4 t^{6} e^{4 t^{6}} + e^{4 t^{6}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =16 t^{4} e^{4 t^{6}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} &=8 t,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=4 t^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =(4 t^{6} e^{4 t^{6}} + e^{4 t^{6}})\\cdot (8 t)+(16 t^{4} e^{4 t^{6}})\\cdot (4 t^{3}) \\\\  & =8 t e^{4 t^{6}} + (32 t^{7} e^{4 t^{6}}) + (64 t^{7} e^{4 t^{6}}) \\\\  & =8 t (12 t^{6} + 1) e^{4 t^{6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561366 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41d97176-e025-5b4c-b7b0-083e3d586b5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 t^{6} e^{t^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561334} {:answer/id #uuid "6c364802-b683-5589-9cbc-78d6e2193cf5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 t^{6} e^{t^{5}} + 2 t (t^{5} e^{t^{5}} + e^{t^{5}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561345} {:answer/id #uuid "b8b596cf-1a25-54ec-ac13-3566c265de83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- t (5 t^{5} + 2) e^{t^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561363} {:answer/id #uuid "c3ce3c3d-48ea-5361-8456-9d24ca042189" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t (5 t^{5} + 2) e^{t^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561369} {:answer/id #uuid "e85d9162-b4d4-547e-bd9a-0d23fbc8ff6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 t (t^{5} e^{t^{5}} + e^{t^{5}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561377}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3ce3c3d-48ea-5361-8456-9d24ca042189" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t (5 t^{5} + 2) e^{t^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561369} :answer-field/id #uuid "95940820-fd45-5f5b-99f8-92f8a12c3bad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561357}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bf7fe78b-1c1d-5127-987b-8cd96d86abd1" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x e^{x y},$ $x=t^{2}$ and $y=t^{3},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=x y e^{x y} + e^{x y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x^{2} e^{x y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =t^{5} e^{t^{5}} + e^{t^{5}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =t^{4} e^{t^{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} &=2 t,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=3 t^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =(t^{5} e^{t^{5}} + e^{t^{5}})\\cdot (2 t)+(t^{4} e^{t^{5}})\\cdot (3 t^{2}) \\\\  & =2 t e^{t^{5}} + (2 t^{6} e^{t^{5}}) + (3 t^{6} e^{t^{5}}) \\\\  & =t (5 t^{5} + 2) e^{t^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561368 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "034ddcd1-8433-5781-9469-3da41704071a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 (t - 3) ((t - 3)^{3} (t - 1) + (t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} + 1) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561311} {:answer/id #uuid "0ce87af5-550b-5dba-a26e-ec8e204c383b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (t - 3)^{4} (2 t - 2) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}} + (2 t - 6) ((t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}} + e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561314} {:answer/id #uuid "162afb4b-a2e1-57a0-9bd7-26af13560665" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2 t - 6) ((t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}} + e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561316} {:answer/id #uuid "2b8a29c8-9053-5cd1-9ac6-2e79e49f6003" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(t - 3)^{4} (2 t - 2) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561325} {:answer/id #uuid "73b29452-f6b2-5756-85ed-42f37daa52fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 (t - 3) ((t - 3)^{3} (t - 1) + (t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} + 1) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "034ddcd1-8433-5781-9469-3da41704071a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 (t - 3) ((t - 3)^{3} (t - 1) + (t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} + 1) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561311} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b3a4874-dfd3-558e-abb9-8d0f1d1e6fd4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561330}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c1b4aee3-81b2-5ef4-a432-21293ceb4d7a" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x e^{x y},$ $x=(t - 3)^{2}$ and $y=(t - 1)^{2},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=x y e^{x y} + e^{x y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x^{2} e^{x y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}} + e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =(t - 3)^{4} e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} &=2 t - 6,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=2 t - 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =((t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}} + e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}})\\cdot (2 t - 6)+((t - 3)^{4} e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}})\\cdot (2 t - 2) \\\\  & =(2 t - 6) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}} + ((t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} (2 t - 6) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}) + ((t - 3)^{4} (2 t - 2) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}) \\\\  & =2 (t - 3) ((t - 3)^{3} (t - 1) + (t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} + 1) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561373 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28864dae-edc6-5897-84e2-b4f8f19a9ad8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (2 t - 1)^{6} (8 t - 8) e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}} + 6 (2 t - 1)^{2} ((2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3} e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}} + e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561324} {:answer/id #uuid "2cd50b34-1d20-57d9-b5aa-2865814b40a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 (2 t - 1)^{2} ((2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3} e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}} + e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561326} {:answer/id #uuid "37d75164-96de-5488-990b-58d49b5c3a9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2 t - 1)^{6} (8 t - 8) e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561329} {:answer/id #uuid "3f319f38-17f2-56c6-9ef0-8a9cbad2f14d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 (2 t - 1)^{2} (12 (t - 1)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3} + 4 (t - 1) (2 t - 1)^{4} + 3) e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561331} {:answer/id #uuid "4a217e14-3bda-5454-bcca-c0092a1651a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 (2 t - 1)^{2} (12 (t - 1)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3} + 4 (t - 1) (2 t - 1)^{4} + 3) e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a217e14-3bda-5454-bcca-c0092a1651a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 (2 t - 1)^{2} (12 (t - 1)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3} + 4 (t - 1) (2 t - 1)^{4} + 3) e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561338} :answer-field/id #uuid "d061cc16-2e62-5867-ac53-ca52bd6a819a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561370}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "df6ac8b1-d356-59b7-bc1d-0aa4d063c094" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x e^{x y},$ $x=(2 t - 1)^{3}$ and $y=(2 t - 2)^{2},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=x y e^{x y} + e^{x y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x^{2} e^{x y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3} e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}} + e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =(2 t - 1)^{6} e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} &=6 (2 t - 1)^{2},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=8 t - 8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =((2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3} e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}} + e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}})\\cdot (6 (2 t - 1)^{2})+((2 t - 1)^{6} e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}})\\cdot (8 t - 8) \\\\  & =6 (2 t - 1)^{2} e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}} + (6 (2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{5} e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}}) + ((2 t - 1)^{6} (8 t - 8) e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}}) \\\\  & =2 (2 t - 1)^{2} (12 (t - 1)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3} + 4 (t - 1) (2 t - 1)^{4} + 3) e^{(2 t - 2)^{2} (2 t - 1)^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable"}]}
